WEBVTT

00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:06.640
Everything started on Mars.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:11.780
And everything's about to end, I think.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:14.540
It looks like we'll be fumbling around,

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:16.120
making a racket until the very end.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:19.080
In some ways that's fitting for us, I guess.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:02:00.680
"For the Lady We Will Meet Someday"

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:04.610
Hey, what the hell is going on here?

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:06.700
Are they withdrawing?

00:02:07.010 --> 00:02:09.520
That's right. There's no point in continued fighting for now.

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:13.940
With Akito-kun and Inez-san down below, you can't use the phase transition cannon, right?

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:17.320
Guess we'll have to wait and see how this works out.

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:19.390
Akito...

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.150
How deep is this thing?

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:27.200
According to our research, it's about ten kilometers deep,

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.210
with distortion fields every eight hundred meters.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:33.940
Who was the Doctor talking about greeting?

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:34.630
I don't know.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:36.530
Ai-chan?

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:39.180
I see!

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:40.430
Cherry Icee.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:41.450
I understand. That's why the Doctor was acting a little strange.

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:41.910
I see.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:42.700
I understand. That's why the Doctor was acting a little strange.

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:43.210
Cherry Icee.

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:43.970
I understand. That's why the Doctor was acting a little strange.

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:44.420
I see.

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:44.960
I understand. That's why the Doctor was acting a little strange.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:45.150
But how can you say that it is Ai so easily?

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:45.690
Cherry Icee.

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:46.290
But how can you say that it is Ai so easily?

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:49.460
I see. Cherry Icee.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:51.570
Wait a minute, wait a minute, wait a minute!

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:54.290
What are you all getting excited about?

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:55.830
Who is this Ai-chan?!

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:57.240
Let me explain.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:57.800
Proxy
Inez
Blocking
Communication

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:00.170
Since the Explaining Lady has shut her transmission,

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:01.070
Proxy

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:02.050
I will substitute.

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:02.360
Proxy

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:08.580
Ai-chan is a girl that Akito-san got to know before he boson jumped from Mars to Earth.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:09.010
Proxy

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:12.670
This girl is one of the sources of his psychological trauma.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.130
But Ai-chan was not dead.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:17.660
Onii-chan isn't here yet.

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:20.000
Hold on, he will be soon.

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:21.050
Okay.

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:24.640
Probably, the many distortion fields inside the ruin

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:27.440
are blocking his path, making it really difficult for him.

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:29.820
What's wrong?

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:31.710
You smell really nice, auntie.

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:33.850
I'm not sure I like being called auntie.

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:34.750
Like mommy.

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:36.900
You smell just like my mommy!

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:39.110
Mommy's so mean, you know?

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:41.320
She went to sleep with everyone else when it went boom.

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:46.240
Then Onii-chan started shining really bright and looked like he went away and then...

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:52.290
Wait! Onii-chan! Onii-chan! Onii-chan!

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.800
A free-falling object is approaching from above!

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:01.350
What is it?

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:02.550
It appears to be...

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:06.060
A Chulip!

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:08.380
Damage to starboard!

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:12.300
Field strength down twenty percent.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:13.390
We were hit with a gravity blast!

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:14.270
Enemy?

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:19.180
Analysis of enemy strength complete.

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:21.190
Two new phase transition core powered battleships.

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:23.600
One is the Nadesico!

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:24.830
Nadesico?!

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:28.290
Did you hear that, Captain?! Now we can return the favor from...

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:29.250
I'm fully aware!

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:32.170
Okay, let's see what that dashing man of action does this time!

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:35.870
Kannazuki is moving ahead, Sir.

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:37.880
Dispatch to Kannazuki.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:38.240
Aye.

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:41.670
Prepare humanoid and arthropodal fighters for immediate launch.

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:44.940
Auntie!

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:46.050
It's all right.

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:48.010
Nadesico?

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:48.990
Inez-san!

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:52.890
It's terrible! A Chulip arrived and the Jovians suddenly attacked!

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:54.590
I see.

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:58.690
The ruins were reinvigorated due to a boson jump nearby.

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:00.900
Ai-chan?

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:03.660
Inez-san? Inez-san?

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:05.700
Inez-san!

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:07.580
Mobile enemy weapons approaching.

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:10.360
We'll worry about the enemy at hand first.

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:11.470
Ryoko-chan!

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:13.710
Gotcha, just let me at them.

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:15.470
Prepare gravity blast cannon!

00:05:15.470 --> 00:05:16.000
Aye!

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:20.170
Enemy Gekigan type units approaching via boson jump.

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:28.470
Auntie, I'm scared, I'm scared!

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:30.390
Hurry, Akito-kun!

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:34.140
This is the last one. Give it full power!

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:34.650
Roger!

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:36.440
I'm coming, Ai-chan!

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:37.440
Ai-chan!

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:40.830
Onii-chan! Onii-chan! Hurry, Onii-chan!

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:44.120
I don't wanna, auntie!

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:46.820
I still haven't met Onii-chan! I still haven't...

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:47.910
You will.

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:50.570
Maybe not now, but you will some day!

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:53.030
You're a strong girl, aren't you?

00:05:53.030 --> 00:05:54.130
That's why you need to believe.

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:55.750
That's why you can't forget.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:59.670
His face, his voice, no matter what happens.

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:02.590
Please don't forget, never forget this.

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:03.490
Okay.

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:08.140
I feel like I'm talking to my mommy.

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:12.070
Oh, right. They asked me to give this to you.

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:14.920
When I got here I was supposed to...

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:26.920
An entrusted item...

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:34.170
Ai-chan!

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:37.120
Inez-san, where is Ai-chan?

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:39.180
You just missed her.

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:43.050
I told you to hurry, but maybe it was meant to be like this.

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:44.800
Inez-san...

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:47.840
The "l" in Inez is pronounced "Ai" in the alphabet.

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:52.880
That child was drawn into Akito's boson jump back in the colony.

00:06:54.770 --> 00:06:57.090
She ended up in ancient Mars.

00:06:57.650 --> 00:07:01.000
She was sent back by the people who built these ruins.

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:04.600
But thanks to all the mess just now, she jumped again,

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:06.740
and ended up in the middle of a desert twenty years ago.

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:10.180
Back when all our memories were joined together,

00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:13.430
you saw this, my memories, my past.

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:14.590
Inez-san...

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:16.840
You saw it too, Akatsuki-kun?

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:18.010
Yeah.

00:07:18.510 --> 00:07:20.010
All the other pilots,

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:22.120
along with the Captain and Ruri-chan, saw it as well, right?

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:22.750
Yes.

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:27.040
Inez-san, you recovered your memory back then, didn't you?

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:27.670
I did.

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:30.900
The little girl lost all her memory

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:32.690
from the shock of being left in the desert.

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:37.240
She was picked up by some Nergal workers in the area, and...

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:38.030
That's enough!

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:39.570
I knew all this.

00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:41.940
I knew it in my mind, but couldn't bring myself together to say it!

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:44.860
I'm sorry, Ai-chan. I'm sorry for not being able to help you.

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:49.550
It's great to finally be able to meet you, onii-chan.

00:07:53.090 --> 00:07:55.370
I get it, I get it, I get it!

00:07:55.960 --> 00:08:00.040
So it's the time paradox thing, all Sci-Fi and stuff, right?

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:02.460
So just leave that aside and give us some cover!

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:05.240
We're being hammered by everybody here!

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:09.750
That's true. Kakitsubata is suffering a brutal beating.

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:16.930
The hunter of two hares loses both like a seat between two chairs!

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:22.100
Instead of the formidable Nadesico, we'll first dispose of the other ship!

00:08:22.570 --> 00:08:23.410
Saburota!

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:24.520
I'm on it.

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:27.250
Gekigan Punch!

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:30.240
Get out, Erina-kun!

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:30.860
But...

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:32.280
Just run for it!

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:41.370
Gekigan Beam!

00:08:44.450 --> 00:08:45.380
The Kakitsubata...

00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:46.750
Sunk?

00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:48.440
Erina Won...

00:08:48.740 --> 00:08:50.580
While still struggling to realize her dreams, she perishes on Mars.

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:51.810
I haven't perished yet!

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:52.990
Rest in...

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:54.760
Hey! Stop that crying, damn it!

00:08:55.350 --> 00:08:57.170
Oh, why does it have to be like this?!

00:08:58.250 --> 00:08:59.350
It's my fault.

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:02.180
Please, Akito-san, don't blame yourself.

00:09:02.590 --> 00:09:06.270
The Ai that I met two years ago was a little girl.

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:09.230
But she was sent back to the past because of me,

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:11.230
and forced to go through so much suffering.

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:14.100
And ended up being such a quibbling old auntie.

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:16.470
But you can't change anything back.

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:17.120
That's right!

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:19.540
Come on now, Akito-san. Have a rice ball now!

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:22.090
You're just feeling down because you're hungry!

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:23.610
Stuff it in! Stuff it in!

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:25.710
What are you doing to me?!

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:26.450
Eat it! Eat it!

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:32.500
I can't keep weeping when everyone's working hard.

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:34.180
Please watch over me closely, onii-chan.

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:36.750
I'll carry out your wishes!

00:09:40.520 --> 00:09:42.060
What's the status of the enemy ship?

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:45.800
They have remained silent since descending into the ruin depths.

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:46.860
No movement.

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:48.740
Dispatch to the enemy ship!

00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:48.900
Aye, Sir.

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:52.330
Abandon the ruins at once and surrender immediately!

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:55.200
You will be given thirty minutes to comply.

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:58.150
If you do, you have my word that l,
Major Tsukiomi Genichirou of the Yuujin Forces,

00:09:58.150 --> 00:09:59.920
will guarantee your safety.

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:00.790
That's all.

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:05.420
Well, it certainly looks like we are completely cornered.

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:06.620
What do we do, Captain?

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:08.210
We will not surrender!

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:11.200
We have no intention of letting them have the ruin in any case,

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:13.130
so let's punch through with a big bang!

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:16.840
Are you all right, Ken?

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:19.390
But we're getting nowhere against this many.

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:24.310
It appears that the moon will be where you will perish.

00:10:24.770 --> 00:10:26.690
Die, Gekiganger!

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:45.910
Gekigan Sword!

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:56.230
This is nothing compared to true Hell.

00:10:56.790 --> 00:11:00.010
Get yourselves together, Ken, Akira!

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:01.470
Joe!

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:03.350
Umitsubame Joe, you're alive!

00:11:03.730 --> 00:11:04.430
Joe!

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:07.350
Let's do it, partners.

00:11:07.610 --> 00:11:10.110
If we can inflict Shogun more damage now, it will be the end.

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:12.870
Isn't it so convenient, dying and then resurrecting.

00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:15.190
Use this, Gekiganger V!

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:18.420
Gekigan Sword!

00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:22.030
Hyper Passion Slash!

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:26.570
Was what you believed in this hollow?

00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:27.960
Stare.

00:11:28.270 --> 00:11:30.460
Oh, it's you, Yukina-chan.

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:32.300
Why are you weeping like that?

00:11:32.300 --> 00:11:34.060
I don't think that's how an adult is supposed to behave.

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:35.660
It's okay if I am a child.

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:36.380
Of course it isn't!

00:11:36.980 --> 00:11:38.830
I... I...

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:41.290
I'm going to be Minato-san's groom!

00:11:54.110 --> 00:11:54.980
What?!

00:11:55.330 --> 00:11:56.940
Self-destruct?

00:11:57.170 --> 00:11:59.600
We'll overload the four phase transition engines of the Nadesico

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:01.400
and blow up the ruins!

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:02.640
Yeah, this will work!

00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:04.150
Hey, wait just a minute here!

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:06.430
Are you going make everyone here sacrifice themselves for this?

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:07.290
Of course not.

00:12:08.020 --> 00:12:10.210
The only person that'll stay behind will be me, the Captain.

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:11.670
Wait a second...

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:16.060
Hold on, Yurika. You want to die doing this?!

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:18.130
Don't worry, I won't die.

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:18.660
Baka!

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:21.470
Do you have any idea what you are saying?!

00:12:21.830 --> 00:12:22.790
Baka, you'll die.

00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:25.630
No, I won't die! I will not die!

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:26.600
Yes, you will!

00:12:26.900 --> 00:12:27.510
No, I won't!

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:28.430
Yes, you will!

00:12:28.550 --> 00:12:30.340
No, I won't, I won't, I won't!

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:32.590
Yes, you will die, and that's that, Baka!

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:36.800
What?!

00:12:38.720 --> 00:12:40.460
You made her cry!

00:12:40.460 --> 00:12:41.610
What the hell are you people saying?!

00:12:42.340 --> 00:12:45.240
The war would end if the ruins were gone.

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:46.360
But...

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:49.030
Would we really be able to destroy it even if we self-destructed?

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:52.460
Look, this is when you should count on Nergal.

00:12:52.460 --> 00:12:53.890
We won't let anything bad happen.

00:12:53.890 --> 00:12:54.960
That's right, Captain.

00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:58.380
Look who's talking. You just lost the Kakitsubata.

00:12:59.520 --> 00:13:02.510
Oh, don't pay any heed to what a child murmurs out loud.

00:13:03.100 --> 00:13:04.930
Regardless, no self-destruction!

00:13:05.270 --> 00:13:06.350
Why not?!

00:13:06.350 --> 00:13:06.800
Because I say so!

00:13:07.570 --> 00:13:10.220
We would be able to save the universe!

00:13:10.690 --> 00:13:14.300
We could do this even through we let all those people on Mars die!

00:13:15.110 --> 00:13:17.000
But you would die.

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:18.990
Well, that might not be the case.

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:23.400
According to Inez-san's explanation, these ruins are like a huge time machine.

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:23.980
Strategy-planning is although confidential, but by Ruri-san's request, this time will be an exception.
Urgent Broadcasting

00:13:23.980 --> 00:13:26.070
So if we blow up the ruins,

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:29.550
then all the boson jumping that took place in past, present, and future will all be voided,

00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:30.860
as if none of it took place.

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:34.590
So how far back would we back track after that?

00:13:38.510 --> 00:13:39.520
That's not me.

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:41.170
Then...

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:48.220
You're...

00:13:51.920 --> 00:13:56.750
Being myself, being myself,

00:13:56.750 --> 00:14:00.370
I want to find a future all my own...

00:14:00.370 --> 00:14:02.360
No, no, you don't do things like self-destruction.

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:03.320
V!

00:14:05.630 --> 00:14:06.330
Admiral?!

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:08.390
We never suspected you were still alive.

00:14:08.390 --> 00:14:11.200
Are you disappointed that I'm still alive?

00:14:12.270 --> 00:14:13.790
I met him inside the ruins.

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:16.720
He was saved by Battas and interned until now.

00:14:18.110 --> 00:14:18.630
V!

00:14:19.270 --> 00:14:20.290
But why, Admiral?!

00:14:20.530 --> 00:14:22.360
Admiral, why shouldn't we self-destruct?

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:25.270
Because it's self-destructive. It's stupid.

00:14:25.270 --> 00:14:25.720
No way!

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:29.090
I wanted to save everybody with the ship like you did, Admiral...

00:14:33.240 --> 00:14:34.250
Ruri-chan...

00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:35.890
I'm against it.

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:36.460
But...

00:14:36.910 --> 00:14:39.110
If we destroy the ruins, then history will be rewritten.

00:14:39.110 --> 00:14:40.980
There would be no war, a clean slate.

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:44.690
But we will lose something that's very dear to us as well.

00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:52.020
Two minutes until the retrieval of the ruin unit.

00:14:52.400 --> 00:14:55.220
Does it still work even if we detach it and take it in?

00:14:55.220 --> 00:14:58.760
Supposedly time and space means nothing to the ruins.

00:14:59.530 --> 00:15:01.070
I don't quite get it.

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:04.870
Maybe it's that even while apart, our hearts are still one.

00:15:05.570 --> 00:15:06.620
Minato-san!

00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:09.490
I'm so sorry. Did I make you worry?

00:15:09.490 --> 00:15:11.020
But is it all right?

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:13.090
It's Yukina-chan.

00:15:14.020 --> 00:15:16.450
She said she would become my groom.

00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:18.760
I've go to pull myself together,

00:15:19.070 --> 00:15:21.450
for the sake of that little screwball we have with us.

00:15:21.970 --> 00:15:22.730
Yes, you're right.

00:15:23.430 --> 00:15:25.520
Ruri-chan, it's about time, you can come here.

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:26.400
Yes.

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:29.530
What's most important to me...

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:34.080
My life on board the Nadesico for more than a year.

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:37.130
All I have are these memories.

00:15:37.800 --> 00:15:41.380
Not memories that were given to me, but memories that I won.

00:15:41.630 --> 00:15:44.630
That's all I have. I won't let that go.

00:15:45.120 --> 00:15:50.390
Captain, what's the most important thing for you?

00:15:51.120 --> 00:15:53.600
You granted them thirty minutes? You're too soft, Tsukiomi!

00:15:53.920 --> 00:15:57.530
While the enemy force might be feeble, they have taken shelter inside the city.

00:15:57.530 --> 00:15:58.770
That's why you must rush ahead!

00:16:00.410 --> 00:16:03.330
I'm just not used to this outfit.

00:16:04.580 --> 00:16:06.270
You look splendid in it, Captain.

00:16:06.590 --> 00:16:07.150
Shut up!

00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:09.610
Five enemy Gekigan-type units approaching!

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:12.490
Well, we'll take care of those somehow.

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:13.820
You just take care of things on your end!

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:14.540
Yes.

00:16:15.010 --> 00:16:16.720
Now, let's get started.

00:16:16.720 --> 00:16:19.510
Are you sure we'll be able to make the Nadesico jump?

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:20.960
Theoretically.

00:16:21.390 --> 00:16:25.380
The ruins are entirely composed of the same material as the Chulip Crystals.

00:16:25.760 --> 00:16:27.180
Are you ready, Ruri-chan?

00:16:27.480 --> 00:16:27.840
Yes.

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:29.300
Start the sequence, Erina-san!

00:16:31.230 --> 00:16:33.250
Choosing memories over world peace.

00:16:33.740 --> 00:16:36.140
In the end, everyone acts according to their own agenda.

00:16:36.710 --> 00:16:39.070
I guess you can call it enlightened egocentrism.

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:51.110
Unable to create stable boson field.

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:57.650
You two, kiss each other.

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:02.650
Since we don't have a Chulip standing by with an open field,

00:17:02.650 --> 00:17:07.000
we'll need to create a really large field in order for a ship of this size to jump.

00:17:07.630 --> 00:17:13.080
In order to do that, we'll need to have electric, or membrane to membrane, contact among ourselves.

00:17:13.080 --> 00:17:14.690
So, kiss?

00:17:14.690 --> 00:17:14.930
Exactly.

00:17:15.350 --> 00:17:17.850
The Nadesico will be in a pinch unless you hurry.

00:17:18.340 --> 00:17:18.980
No!

00:17:19.610 --> 00:17:20.480
Yurika...

00:17:20.480 --> 00:17:22.690
I said no and I meant no! Definitely not!

00:17:22.990 --> 00:17:25.190
Really, this is no time to start pouting.

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:26.970
That's right. It can't be helped.

00:17:26.970 --> 00:17:27.770
It can't be helped?!

00:17:28.330 --> 00:17:31.060
Why don't you just go ahead and kiss Inez-san instead, then!

00:17:32.050 --> 00:17:33.820
Gekigan Beam!

00:17:34.350 --> 00:17:35.300
Whoops!

00:17:35.960 --> 00:17:37.940
You're as slow as ever, you oaf!

00:17:40.670 --> 00:17:41.370
Whoa!

00:17:41.840 --> 00:17:46.290
So we've found out that only people born on Mars are capable of boson jumping?

00:17:46.670 --> 00:17:48.210
Tenkawa, the Doctor, and the Captain.

00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:51.130
It's probably because the nanomachines were influenced

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:53.770
by the ruins to re-write the DNA information of all Martians.

00:17:54.020 --> 00:17:55.940
It changed their bodies so that they can withstand the jumps.

00:17:56.250 --> 00:17:57.300
That's probably the case.

00:17:57.370 --> 00:17:58.140
What a deal.

00:17:58.450 --> 00:18:02.560
One of those Martians has run off while the other is chasing her.

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:03.470
What's that about?

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:06.470
I must admit, this ship is one interesting place.

00:18:07.380 --> 00:18:08.160
Onii-chan...

00:18:09.180 --> 00:18:12.860
I'm going to Earth with Minato-san, so please...

00:18:13.550 --> 00:18:15.280
So please watch over me, onii-chan!

00:18:15.630 --> 00:18:16.740
Hey! Get out now!

00:18:17.390 --> 00:18:19.060
Just get out of there! I said get out, damn it!

00:18:19.060 --> 00:18:20.070
Seiya-san!

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:21.880
You came just in time!

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:24.910
I have no idea why, but the Captain's in your Aestivalis.

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:26.290
Hey, Yurika!

00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:28.790
Get down from there. You can't pilot that.

00:18:28.790 --> 00:18:29.750
Without an IFS...

00:18:34.620 --> 00:18:37.210
What's the Captain doing with an IFS?

00:18:37.210 --> 00:18:38.170
Stupid.

00:18:38.580 --> 00:18:39.840
Jump, Akito-kun!

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:42.990
Visualize the inside of the Aestivalis!

00:18:43.320 --> 00:18:43.950
Yurika...

00:18:48.110 --> 00:18:49.450
No!

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:50.730
Hey, watch it!

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:51.950
No!

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:52.860
Stop it, Yurika.

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:54.260
Go away!

00:18:54.260 --> 00:18:55.280
Go away where?

00:18:55.320 --> 00:18:56.490
You jerk, Akito!

00:18:59.460 --> 00:19:00.620
What is that?

00:19:00.990 --> 00:19:03.610
Sounds like a couple fighting it out over the comm channel.

00:19:04.270 --> 00:19:04.980
Move over.

00:19:04.980 --> 00:19:05.570
No!

00:19:05.570 --> 00:19:06.310
Come on!

00:19:06.310 --> 00:19:06.960
I don't want to.

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:09.290
What are you thinking?!

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:10.610
Stop being so proud!

00:19:10.900 --> 00:19:14.290
But you have Inez-san... Ai-chan...

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:16.380
What the hell are you saying?!

00:19:16.760 --> 00:19:19.430
You're feeling guilty over what happened to Inez-san, right?

00:19:19.810 --> 00:19:22.300
That's why I tried to turn back time.

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:23.500
Baka!

00:19:25.570 --> 00:19:29.940
By the way, I've been relaying the feed from the Tenkawa Aestivalis for the Jovians to listen.

00:19:30.530 --> 00:19:33.900
A quarrel between lovers to decide the fate of the universe.

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:34.330
Yes.

00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:37.450
That's mean. You didn't have to hit me like that.

00:19:38.200 --> 00:19:42.300
Yurika, I watched the last episode of Gekiganger 3.

00:19:43.720 --> 00:19:46.360
Oh, it was a terrible episode.

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:49.870
Just god-awful.

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:53.000
But as god-awful as it was, I felt shivers going down my spine.

00:19:53.610 --> 00:19:57.940
Watching Gekiganger 3 and Gekiganger V
fight alongside each other...

00:19:58.250 --> 00:20:00.760
So, you do like the show after all?

00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:04.690
I want to believe in how I was so attached to Gekiganger.

00:20:05.480 --> 00:20:08.170
Believe in the part of myself that has faith in hot-blooded passion.

00:20:08.930 --> 00:20:09.430
That's why...

00:20:10.210 --> 00:20:12.200
That's why Akito's in love with me!

00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:15.160
Just as I was about to get to the grand scale of things!

00:20:16.180 --> 00:20:17.530
That's right. You got a problem with that?

00:20:17.890 --> 00:20:18.440
No.

00:20:19.290 --> 00:20:20.360
What about you?

00:20:20.840 --> 00:20:22.930
Me? I...

00:20:24.190 --> 00:20:25.790
I love you very much, Akito!

00:20:26.470 --> 00:20:27.750
That's the first time I heard that.

00:20:28.280 --> 00:20:29.000
No way!

00:20:29.360 --> 00:20:30.130
It's true.

00:20:30.400 --> 00:20:31.450
No way!

00:20:31.450 --> 00:20:32.410
Really!

00:20:32.410 --> 00:20:33.400
No way!

00:20:33.400 --> 00:20:33.790
Really!

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:35.370
No way!

00:20:35.370 --> 00:20:36.030
Yes...

00:20:39.370 --> 00:20:41.260
I love you, Akito.

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:47.050
So, all that said and done,

00:20:47.310 --> 00:20:51.380
I wonder if kissing was really essential for them to boson jump.

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:56.320
Inez-san wouldn't explain any further, other then to say that I would know once I grew older.

00:20:57.500 --> 00:21:00.820
In the end, the big mysteries remained as they did before.

00:21:01.520 --> 00:21:03.860
The plate that Inez-san was given...

00:21:04.090 --> 00:21:06.530
The ancient civilization that resided on Mars long ago...

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:10.450
Still, we had the calculation unit from the ruins

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:13.250
sent far, far away on board the Nadesico.

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:17.940
The war between Jupiter and Earth will probably go on,

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:20.560
but now they can only glare at each other for the time being.

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:25.990
But we have to wait for another opportunity to go into what happens later.
